<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Feed group buys 56,000T US corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Feed group buys 56,000T US corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Members Feed Industry Group bought a 56,000-tonne shipment of U.S. No.2 corn from Mitsui at a tender on Wednesday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The feed group's main buyers are Taiwan's Formosa Oilseed, Fomau Cereal, Morn Sun Feed Mill and Shin Tai Industry.</p>
<p>The shipment was bought on an FOB basis with freight fixed at US$11.09 per tonne from MIT.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Tonnage    Date/Location  Prices/Futures</p>
<p>				   Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> 31,500     June 16-30     US$136.70</p>
<p> 24,500     June 16-30     46.00 US cents/July</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
